{
  "schema": "formulate/reference-polymers/1",
  "description": "Repeat-unit structures and measured bulk properties for common homopolymers, split into a set used to fit the group-contribution coefficients and a set held out from fitting entirely.",
  "provenance": "Commonly tabulated handbook values (Brandrup/Immergut Polymer Handbook and the standard polymer-physics texts) recorded to the nearest kelvin and the nearest 0.005 g/cm^3. These are reference values for fitting and regression guarding, NOT a curated scientific benchmark; verify against a primary source before drawing a scientific conclusion from an error computed against them.",
  "caveats": [
    "A glass transition is a kinetic event, not a phase transition: a reported Tg depends on cooling rate and on whether it was measured by DSC, DMA or dilatometry, and values for the same polymer differ between compilations by 5-10 K.",
    "Tg values are for the atactic or otherwise conventionally amorphous form. Tacticity moves Tg by tens of kelvin (isotactic PMMA is roughly 60 K below atactic, syndiotactic roughly 20 K above), so a stereoregular polymer is outside this set.",
    "Densities are for the AMORPHOUS phase at 298 K. A semicrystalline sample is denser than this in proportion to its crystallinity, which depends on processing rather than on chemistry.",
    "Tg values here are the high-molar-mass limit. Below roughly 20 kg/mol chain ends depress Tg measurably (Fox-Flory), and the depression is polymer-specific."
  ],
  "splits": {
    "fit": "used to fit the coefficients; in-sample error on these is not evidence of anything",
    "validation": "never used to fit a coefficient or to choose a descriptor; the error on these is the honest one"
  },
  "van_der_waals_volume": "van_der_waals_volume_a3 is not measured data. It is the geometric van der Waals volume of one interior repeat unit in cubic angstroms, produced by formulate.experts.polymer.repeat_unit_vdw_volume: a 4-mer and a 2-mer are embedded in 3D (ETKDGv3, fixed seed, three conformers, MMFF or UFF relaxed), their grid volumes averaged over conformers, and the difference divided by two. It is cached here only so that fitting the packing factor does not re-embed sixty oligomers on import; deleting the field changes nothing but the time taken. On the simple hydrocarbons it reproduces Bondi's group volumes to within a couple of percent.",
